"Let a clutter $\\mathcal{C}$ **embed** $PG(k-2,2)$ when some subset of $\\mathcal{C}$ is a duplication of the cuboid of $\\operatorname{cocycle}(PG(k-2,2))$. A clutter is **clean tangled** if it is both clean and tangled.\n\n**Projective-geometry embedding conjecture.** Every clean tangled clutter embeds a projective geometry over the two-element field.\n\nThis conjecture is connected with dyadic fractional packings of value two in clean tangled clutters. It is known when the setcore of the clutter has a simplicial convex hull, but remains open in general."